# Dynaverse logon against the stand-ins, for the native client (sfcop --input;
# oracle/driver/run_native.sh --steps): main menu -> MULTIPLAYER -> Game Connections ->
# DYNAVERSE II LOG IN -> the policy notice -> a new account (the client logs on with it at once:
# "Account successfully created!") -> LOGIN -> the Campaign Selector. The data folder's
# servers.json points every service at 127.0.0.1, where sfcop-directory and sfcop-auth run
# (src/net/DIRECTORY_API.md, "The logon, in order"). The selector's rows are not the stand-ins'
# (server/directory/README.md, "Boundary for V2 and V1b"): it opens empty.
#
# Coordinates are the game's display pixels (800x600, the 640x480 menu centred), as in
# menu.steps; calibrated on the native build with --shots captures, 2026-11-08. The fields of the
# login screen drop their placeholder text on the first click, and letters type in lower case.
# The original refuses an email without '@' and a '.' at least four characters from its end
# (STARFLEETOP 0x005DAC19), so the '@' is typed with Shift held. The guest translates a key with
# the Shift state of the moment the game reads it, not the moment it was pressed, and the game
# reads keys a few frames late here: the pauses around the Shift let it catch up first. The
# account is the stand-in's, kept in its memory only, with a throwaway password.

window 60 Starfleet Command

waitmark 60 Select Game
sleep 1500

# --- main menu, "Select Game": MULTIPLAYER opens Game Connections
click 563 348
sleep 5000

# --- Game Connections: DYNAVERSE II, LOG IN opens Dynaverse II Login. The client looks up the
# directory, asks the firewall detector and checks its version; then the policy notice comes up.
click 310 322
sleep 8000

# --- the policy notice: ACCEPT
click 345 442
sleep 2000

# --- E-Mail
click 230 430
sleep 300
key 0x54
key 0x45
key 0x53
key 0x54
key 0x43
key 0x41
key 0x50
key 0x54
key 0x41
key 0x49
key 0x4E
sleep 500
keydown 0x10
sleep 500
key 0x32
sleep 500
keyup 0x10
sleep 500
key 0x45
key 0x58
key 0x41
key 0x4D
key 0x50
key 0x4C
key 0x45
key 0xBE
key 0x54
key 0x45
key 0x53
key 0x54
sleep 300

# --- Password
click 230 453
sleep 300
key 0x54
key 0x48
key 0x52
key 0x4F
key 0x57
key 0x41
key 0x57
key 0x41
key 0x59
sleep 300

# --- Nickname (the field shows OP until clicked)
click 230 476
sleep 300
key 0x54
key 0x45
key 0x53
key 0x54
key 0x43
key 0x41
key 0x50
key 0x54
key 0x41
key 0x49
key 0x4E
sleep 300

# --- CREATE NEW ACCOUNT: the client checks the email by search, then creates the account
click 625 506
sleep 8000

# --- LOGIN: the email check, the challenge, the login and the server's proof; then the
# Campaign Selector
click 297 505
sleep 15000
